\title{PhysioHDEMG: high-density surface EMG motor-unit decomposition}
\description{
PhysioHDEMG decomposes high-density surface EMG (HD-sEMG) electrode-grid
recordings into their constituent motor-unit discharge patterns by
convolutive blind source separation, and summarises the recovered units by
discharge rate, recruitment, decomposition quality, and spatial
action-potential map over the grid. A ground-truth simulator makes the whole
pipeline runnable offline for validation.
}
\section{Simulate ground truth}{

\code{\link[=make_hdemg_sim]{make_hdemg_sim()}} generates a synthetic grid recording with known motor
units (discharge times and spatial maps) for validating a decomposition.
}

\section{Decompose}{

\code{\link[=hdEMGDecompose]{hdEMGDecompose()}} estimates accepted motor-unit pulse trains from a matrix,
an \code{hdemg_sim}, or a \code{PhysioExperiment}.
}

\section{Inspect motor units}{

\code{\link[=muPulseTrains]{muPulseTrains()}} returns the discharges in tidy form, \code{\link[=muFiringStats]{muFiringStats()}}
summarises discharge rate, recruitment, and quality, and
\code{\link[=muActionPotentialMaps]{muActionPotentialMaps()}} recovers the per-unit spatial action-potential map.
}

\section{Validate against a reference}{

\code{\link[=matchMotorUnits]{matchMotorUnits()}} scores a decomposition against a reference set of
discharge patterns with a lag-aware rate of agreement.
}

\section{Ingest and interchange}{

\code{\link[=readHDEMG]{readHDEMG()}} reads an HD-sEMG grid (and any bundled reference decomposition)
from an HDF5 file, and \code{\link[=hdemgToPhysioExperiment]{hdemgToPhysioExperiment()}} wraps a matrix in the
shared ecosystem data model.
}

\section{Where to go next}{

Conventional EMG features (envelopes, amplitude, spectral indices) live in
the sibling \code{PhysioEMG} package; the shared \code{PhysioExperiment} data model and
provenance come from \code{PhysioCore}. See \code{vignette("hdemg-decomposition", package = "PhysioHDEMG")} for an end-to-end walk-through.
}

